{"id":"death-spiritual","name":"Death, Spiritual","aliases":["Death"],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:death-spiritual"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Death","text":"May be simply defined as the termination of life. It is represented under a variety of aspects in Scripture: (1.) “The dust shall return to the earth as it was” (Eccl. 12:7). (2.) “Thou takest away their breath, they die” (Ps. 104:29). (3.) It is the dissolution of “our earthly house of this tabernacle” (2 Cor. 5:1); the “putting off this tabernacle” (2 Pet. 1:13, 14). (4.) Being “unclothed” (2 Cor. 5:3, 4). (5.) “Falling on sleep” (Ps. 76:5; Jer. 51:39; Acts 13:36; 2 Pet. 3:9. (6.) “I go whence I shall not return” (Job 10:21); “Make me to know mine end” (Ps. 39:4); “to depart” (Phil. 1:23). The grave is represented as “the gates of death” (Job 38:17; Ps. 9:13; 107:18). The gloomy silence of the grave is spoken of under the figure of the “shadow of death” (Jer. 2:6). Death is the effect of sin (Heb. 2:14), and not a “debt of nature.” It is but once (9:27), universal (Gen. 3:19), …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G3498","lemma":"νεκρός","xlit":"nekrós","gloss":"dead","kjv":"dead","count":10,"share":0.42},{"strong":"G2222","lemma":"ζωή","xlit":"zōḗ","gloss":"life","kjv":"life","count":6,"share":0.25},{"strong":"G3900","lemma":"παράπτωμα","xlit":"paráptōma","gloss":"a side-slip","kjv":"fall, fault, offence, sin","count":4,"share":0.17},{"strong":"G2288","lemma":"θάνατος","xlit":"thánatos","gloss":"death","kjv":"X deadly, death","count":5,"share":0.21},{"strong":"G2198","lemma":"ζάω","xlit":"záō","gloss":"to live","kjv":"life, live, quick","count":5,"share":0.21},{"strong":"G5607","lemma":"ὤν","xlit":"ṓn","gloss":"being","kjv":"be, come, have","count":4,"share":0.17}],"verses":["Luke.15.24","John.5.25","Rom.6.13","Eph.2.1","Eph.2.5","Eph.5.14","Col.2.13","Heb.6.1","Heb.9.14","Rev.3.1","Isa.9.2","Ezek.37.2","Ezek.37.3","Matt.4.16","Luke.1.79","John.3.36","John.5.24","Rom.5.15","Ro